  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Methyl group has <math><mo>+</mo><mtext>I</mtext><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>effect and&nbsp;<math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>group has&nbsp;<math><mo>-</mo><mtext>I</mtext><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>effect<math><mo>.</mo></math> Therefore, in p-nitro toluene the dipole moments of <math><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math>and&nbsp;<math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> groups act in the same direction. So, the resultant dipole moment is additive.<br /><br />i.e., 3.93 + 0.43 = 4.36 debye<br /><br /><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/afndsajfsda.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 492px; height: 262px;\" /></strong>",
